1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,105
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,105 --> 00:00:09,005
This morning the system named no pick, so tonight there is nothing to grade.

3
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:13,740
No setup, no trade, no loss — that is the discipline working.

4
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:18,676
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

5
00:00:18,676 --> 00:00:24,085
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:27,270
On the day, the book is down 346 dollars.

7
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:30,097
BlackRock (BLK) leads, +0.7 percent.

8
00:00:30,097 --> 00:00:32,610
Dollar Tree (DLTR) lags at -4.9.

9
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:36,850
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

10
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:40,377
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

11
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:48,269
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

12
00:00:48,269 --> 00:00:55,444
6 positions, led by BlackRock, ticker BLK, Target, ticker TGT, AppFolio, ticker APPF.

13
00:00:55,444 --> 00:01:06,926
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

14
00:01:06,896 --> 00:01:11,662
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

15
00:01:11,662 --> 00:01:14,045
Every morning OROS proposes.

16
00:01:14,045 --> 00:01:24,513
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

17
00:01:24,513 --> 00:01:28,427
Inside the book today: 2 positions up, 4 down.

18
00:01:28,427 --> 00:01:30,725
Best, BLK at +0.70 percent.

19
00:01:30,725 --> 00:01:32,512
Worst, DLTR at -4.93.

20
00:01:32,512 --> 00:01:37,448
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

21
00:01:37,448 --> 00:01:44,597
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -2.94% per trade over 1269 graded positions.

22
00:01:44,597 --> 00:01:51,576
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 50% position size.

23
00:01:51,576 --> 00:01:56,682
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

24
00:01:56,682 --> 00:02:08,937
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 159 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 50% until the record earns it back.

25
00:02:08,893 --> 00:02:11,077
Over to the sports desk.

26
00:02:11,077 --> 00:02:20,088
Day 91 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

27
00:02:20,088 --> 00:02:26,185
In first place, the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, at 107,364.

28
00:02:26,185 --> 00:02:31,464
Then the index fund, in gray, 9.2 thousand back at 98,115.

29
00:02:31,464 --> 00:02:38,472
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 9.5 thousand back at 97,907.

30
00:02:38,472 --> 00:02:41,020
The race has no finish line.

31
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:45,207
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

32
00:02:45,207 --> 00:02:49,940
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

33
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:51,760
Nothing is restated.

34
00:02:51,760 --> 00:03:00,668
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

35
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:07,965
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

36
00:03:07,965 --> 00:03:10,206
Nothing here is financial advice.

37
00:03:10,206 --> 00:03:13,195
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
